[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8718"] :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=\\pi +{x}_{1}=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi }{3}=-\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-8723/selection/89f3499418add7fd35f70ba0a3ad80398bfdc46652b8b910d7e50d2c0e73fbe9" :answer/id #uuid "2ac14b7d-6456-5ed5-8599-affa671265f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.252" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8723/selection/6e7a175e9295936630e3212eb1b347ba238e8746fc1354a378df41a1250c7464" :answer/id #uuid "c78074c7-aee0-57a3-b4cd-2e072cc4349d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.470" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8723/selection/60e60984e9b751f034667b6cda81b5cb0fd502b88ffe1a1db4d831d23121fee7" :answer/id #uuid "35349218-5f61-53ab-a8d8-05361b8cf6eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3.252" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8723/selection/46d695b9013e8e461408c18b4463f4e6a789255ffadc5adce86a890005ccf4ac" :answer/id #uuid "f1dba3c9-b8e4-54f8-8f67-b029cc48ee8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.252" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8723/selection/8532039fb44a78e420a8b6bde2f4ee7511b7e25290b92f75b4ec4b88e1d7c202" :answer/id #uuid "a083aba3-6982-5c96-863b-ed6feca7ad83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.448" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8723/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb74f0ce-d4d2-56b0-aed4-e2707f19ee51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8723/selection/89f3499418add7fd35f70ba0a3ad80398bfdc46652b8b910d7e50d2c0e73fbe9" :answer-field/choices ["q-8723/selection/89f3499418add7fd35f70ba0a3ad80398bfdc46652b8b910d7e50d2c0e73fbe9" "q-8723/selection/6e7a175e9295936630e3212eb1b347ba238e8746fc1354a378df41a1250c7464" "q-8723/selection/60e60984e9b751f034667b6cda81b5cb0fd502b88ffe1a1db4d831d23121fee7" "q-8723/selection/46d695b9013e8e461408c18b4463f4e6a789255ffadc5adce86a890005ccf4ac" "q-8723/selection/8532039fb44a78e420a8b6bde2f4ee7511b7e25290b92f75b4ec4b88e1d7c202"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8723" :question/id #uuid "55192e08-2b61-54e3-98fa-563835320c08" :question/math-academy-id "q-8723" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions, in radians, of the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-2$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value to $3$ decimal places of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-2)=-1.107\\,148...≈-1.107\\,149\n$$\n\nSince $-1.107\\,149$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-1.107\\,149.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +{x}_{1}=\\pi -1.107\\,148=2.034\\,444.\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-1.107\\,149,2.034\\,444.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈-1.107\\,149\\cdot 2.034\\,444≈-2.252\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8723/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf8592e-1a43-5d65-af3c-9becd79ae8b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8723"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72833/selection/84aaba064027e7eb0bf329f6bc084c93277c0b932bcb0178f06baf24c9b9c48a" :answer/id #uuid "bc9f62f7-f05c-50e1-b434-181b8e288db4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72833/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" :answer/id #uuid "ae462ded-bc71-58a0-a5ab-c9e6daa44990" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72833/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "05c2a9d4-9532-576e-9d67-2a2a730b8f04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72833/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" :answer/id #uuid "df2222f8-6824-591a-8cd8-b7bc8bc5d8b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72833/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198" :answer/id #uuid "1d6228ac-7251-51c1-a08a-62e6730fac97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72833/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fe6e76b5-5bfe-58c6-8028-4c7443f1609e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72833/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" :answer-field/choices ["q-72833/selection/84aaba064027e7eb0bf329f6bc084c93277c0b932bcb0178f06baf24c9b9c48a" "q-72833/selection/e0bd991ac2e2f2a23ec920e03c6d5103be6b20c12a25d724ab290d4ba5292c3e" "q-72833/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-72833/selection/1e940709a1b00fa910544fd0093551b452ea4b241ad5d9959525312e8a27fa19" "q-72833/selection/adbad78d33491a071139fe589fefda7e9ba65cf97ebbcae14d252ac90459e198"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72833" :question/id #uuid "5674b166-f728-5c02-8624-680e618d28d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-72833" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981396/assets/aae559883c97bbd19321d9baeb26fe15e47cced5b072e12100c42aa579c9d02d.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$ Find, in radians, the $x$-coordinate of the point $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The $y$-values of both functions are the same at the intersection point. Equating the two functions gives:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\n$$\n\n Now, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the required domain, and there is only one point of intersection, we conclude that the $x$-coordinate of the intersection point $A$ is $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72833/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71da663-e7a4-5781-973c-5dc7e4deb83f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72833"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321613/field-1/2ab4d887bd03c06472fa528766bb206551766ecc540c0548c4b29ee1879c735d" :answer/id #uuid "c8d4ba09-aeb4-57ea-9d59-dfa5a08cb4c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321613/field-1/d08818d9751d48a05f01ba37497d3da27fbe70f705234d8e06d8830c6b479721" :answer/id #uuid "19cae293-67ed-5504-83e8-3498429d4f9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321613/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b27a8733-fe30-59bd-895e-988598143499" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321613/field-1/2ab4d887bd03c06472fa528766bb206551766ecc540c0548c4b29ee1879c735d" :answer-field/choices ["q-321613/field-1/2ab4d887bd03c06472fa528766bb206551766ecc540c0548c4b29ee1879c735d" "q-321613/field-1/d08818d9751d48a05f01ba37497d3da27fbe70f705234d8e06d8830c6b479721"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321613/field-2/59aed57f41e18b28e62913aef722072df30eb021fdbba674960b6ff4e4b74960" :answer/id #uuid "a5599670-9303-5755-962b-8cc7bd758d6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321613/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "02a68d44-70a5-54dc-ba29-6324239f4829" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321613/field-2/59aed57f41e18b28e62913aef722072df30eb021fdbba674960b6ff4e4b74960" :answer-field/choices ["q-321613/field-2/59aed57f41e18b28e62913aef722072df30eb021fdbba674960b6ff4e4b74960"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321613" :question/id #uuid "9bb80790-0622-5f51-a71a-ae64b246abab" :question/math-academy-id "q-321613" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{3}{2}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(\\frac{3}{2})=0.982\\,793…≈1.0\n$$\n\nSince $1.0$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.0.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +0.982\\,793…≈4.1.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=1.0$ and $x=4.1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321613/field-1" "q-321613/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321613"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321728/field-1/6ca6456073bfb28c32661123002d387a7ae6bca08c5b36e40cc0ac139cfc5c3b" :answer/id #uuid "24ee3171-c990-58c2-86dd-11454e6dc2db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "158" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321728/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e8c1560-6406-56dd-a155-a0967f779be8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321728/field-1/6ca6456073bfb28c32661123002d387a7ae6bca08c5b36e40cc0ac139cfc5c3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-321728/field-1/6ca6456073bfb28c32661123002d387a7ae6bca08c5b36e40cc0ac139cfc5c3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321728/field-2/69f47025f705f62343a80eb35690bbe3c16d2a5e72340f78b6bef11d8f0709ba" :answer/id #uuid "77824142-036a-565d-b480-ab9c4e8341dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "338" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321728/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c205d0dc-c206-56fc-9ba2-b0b446754b53" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321728/field-2/69f47025f705f62343a80eb35690bbe3c16d2a5e72340f78b6bef11d8f0709ba" :answer-field/choices ["q-321728/field-2/69f47025f705f62343a80eb35690bbe3c16d2a5e72340f78b6bef11d8f0709ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321728" :question/id #uuid "fa1833a4-57a9-5cb0-a032-e3e5800c4fc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-321728" :question/problem "Find the solutions **in degrees** to the equation $5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ Round your answers to **the nearest integer**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+2 & =0 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-2 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-0.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-0.4)=-21.8014{…}^{∘}≈-{22.80}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince $-{22.80}^{∘}$ lies outside the domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate solutions in the domain, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={180}^{∘}+(-{21.80}^{∘})≈{158.20}^{∘},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={360}^{∘}+(-{21.80}^{∘})≈{338.20}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions are $x={158}^{∘}$ and $x={338}^{∘}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-321728/field-1" "q-321728/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321728"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
